Description: Modern nftables firewall with GeoBan country blocking
 NFTBan is a modern, high-performance firewall management system for Linux
 servers using nftables with GeoBan country blocking and self-healing monitoring.
 .
 Features include:
 - GeoBan: Country-based IP blocking (ban/unban/whitelist commands)
 - Atomic operations: Zero-downtime firewall updates via netlink
 - Go binaries: 10-60x faster than bash (compiled during package build)
 - 8 security layers (DDoS, port scan, geo-blocking, threat feeds)
 - Commit-confirm recovery (prevents lockout)
 - FHS-compliant with auto-healing health system
 - Integration with Fail2Ban for automatic banning
 - Stats & metrics with HTML/JSON/CSV reporting
 - Advanced inventory system (processes, packages, firewall state)
 - Baseline management with drift detection
 - 6-layer system protection (CPU/RAM/I/O limits)
 - Cryptographic verification and signing
 - Smart mail adapter (auto-detects best transport)
 - Group-based service management via Polkit (no sudo required)
 .
 NOTE: On Ubuntu/Debian, fail2ban is available in default repositories.
 On Rocky/AlmaLinux, enable EPEL and CRB first:
   dnf install -y epel-release && crb enable
   dnf install -y fail2ban-server
